c0-17.7 14.3-32 32-32zm128-64V320c0 17.7-14.3 32-32 32s-32-14.3-32-32V160c0-17.7 14.3-32 32-32s32 14.3 32 32zm64 32c17.7 0 32 14.3 32 32v96c0 17.7-14.3 32-32 32s-32-14.3-32-32V224c0-17.7 14.3-32 32-32zM480 96V320c0 17.7-14.3 32-32 32s-32-14.3-32-32V96c0-17.7 14.3-32 32-32s32 14.3 32 32z"> </path></svg></div><div class="flex-grow-1 ms-2"><a target="_blank" class="accordion-button" href="/horizon/outlook/power-tools-market/mea"><p class="recent_public_media_stats mb-0 text-limit-2 lh-base font-s-14">MEA Power Tools Market Outlook</p></a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="row"><div class="col-lg-9 col-md-8"><div class="row position-relative"><div class="col-xxl-12 col-lg-12 col-md-12 mb-md-4 mb-3"><div class="card card-border mb-0 "><div class="card-body position-relative h-480p pt-   overflow-y-auto overflow-x-hidden text_padding_lt"><div><div class="position-relative reading_full_box over_tbl "><div><h2>U.S. power tools market highlights</h2><ul><li><span>The U.S. power tools market generated a revenue of USD 7,541.4 million in 2025 and is expected to reach USD 15,043.4 million by 2033.</span></li><li><span>The U.S. market is expected to grow at a CAGR of 9.3% from 2026 to 2033.</span></li><li><span>In terms of segment, drills was the largest revenue generating product in 2025.</span></li><li><span>Drills is the most lucrative product segment registering the fastest growth during the forecast period.</span></li></ul><p><br></p><h3>Power tools market data book summary</h3><div class="d-flex justify-content-left ms-8"><table class="table table-striped table-bordered table_hover rounded"><tbody><tr><td>Market revenue in 2025</td><td>USD 7,541.4 million</td></tr><tr><td>Market revenue in 2033</td><td>USD 15,043.4 million</td></tr><tr><td>Growth rate</td><td>9.3% (CAGR from 2026 to 2033)</td></tr><tr><td>Largest segment</td><td>Drills</td></tr><tr><td>Fastest growing segment</td><td>Drills</td></tr><tr><td>Historical data</td><td>2021 - 2024</td></tr><tr><td>Base year</td><td>2025</td></tr><tr><td>Forecast period</td><td>2026 - 2033</td></tr><tr><td>Quantitative units</td><td>Revenue in USD million</td></tr><tr><td>Market segmentation</td><td>Drills, Saws, Wrenches, Grinders, Sanders</td></tr><tr><td>Key market players worldwide</td><td>Emerson Electric Co, Ingersoll Rand Inc, Hitachi Ltd, Makita Corp, Robert Bosch Engineering &amp; Business Solutions, Stanley Black &amp; Decker, Techtronic Industries Co Ltd</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><br></p><h3>Other key industry trends</h3><ul class="second_ul"><li>In terms of revenue, U.S. accounted for 21.7% of the <a class="text_underline" href="https://www.grandviewresearch.com/industry-analysis/power-tools-market" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">power tools market</a> in 2025.</li><li>Country-wise, China is expected to lead the global market in terms of revenue in 2033.</li><li>In North America, U.S. power tools market is projected to lead the regional market in terms of revenue in 2033.</li><li>U.S. is the fastest growing regional market in North America and is projected to reach USD 15,043.4 million by 2033.</li></ul><br></div></div><div class="my-2"><hr class="w-40"/><p>Key Regions:<a class="ms-1" href="/horizon/outlook/power-tools-market/united-states"><span class="text_underline">U.S.</span>, </a><a class="ms-1" href="/horizon/outlook/power-tools-market/uk"><span class="text_underline">UK</span>, </a><a class="ms-1" href="/horizon/outlook/power-tools-market/japan"><span class="text_underline">Japan</span>, </a><a class="ms-1" href="/horizon/outlook/power-tools-market/brazil"><span class="text_underline">Brazil</span>, </a><a class="ms-1" href="/horizon/outlook/power-tools-market/germany"><span class="text_underline">Germany</span></a></p></div><div class="row justify-content-center pb-2"><div class="col-lg-6"><div class="text-center"><div class=""><button class="btn  btn-outline-primary-horizon btn-lg  text-none mt-4 mb-0 ms-0 me-0      bt